      "inferred_worked_solution": "First, notice that $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](images/41/416a18fd3a2a11c7fbb0ce2fdd3ed75b83410396e8ec52b8a7c993745ca81b4d.png)",
